          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "like a scientist, it is equally important to ask interesting questions! Great scientists don’t just answer questions — they ask amazing ones! (Remember last year we had said, “To be a wise person, you must be a whys person”.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.16,
            0.883,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Look at the answers below. Your task is to come up with a curious, creative, and fun question or situations that could lead to these answers. There are never any wrong questions, so let your imagination run wild! Since such exercises might not be very familiar, here is an example to help you! Suppose the answer was ‘just make it half!’ — what all could this be a response to? Well, it could range from “How do we ensure getting equal shares of cake?” to “My essay is too long”, or “I can’t fit this in the envelope” or even “I cannot dance to such a long song”... all very different! So, let’s see what kind of creative questions you can ask!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.374,
            0.865,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Question: _?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.411,
            0.584,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer: Just add some milk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.443,
            0.865,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Question: ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.477,
            0.753,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer: Because the cat’s teeth were crooked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.504,
            0.862,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Question: ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.538,
            0.675,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer: Don’t panic, I have my towel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.569,
            0.862,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Question: ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.602,
            0.42,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer: 42"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.635,
            0.882,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(Please ask a more interesting, and not obvious questions like “What is 32+10?”, or even “What is the answer to life, the universe, and everything?”)"
